course: dictionary
lesson: 12552
title: A formal word: detrimental
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound grown-up because they come from formal writing, like reports, science books and news. «Detrimental» is one of these. You can work it out from the clues around it. «Smoking is detrimental to health» tells you that smoking is bad for your body, so detrimental must mean causing harm.
explain: Look for clues in the words near it. «Pollution has detrimental effects on rivers, and the fish die.» The fish dying is the clue. Something that kills fish is harming the river, so detrimental means harmful.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it in. «Pollution has harmful effects on rivers» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Everyday words for detrimental are harmful and bad for, but detrimental sounds more serious and is used in formal writing.
fact: Detrimental is an adjective, and it means causing harm or damage.
fact: Detrimental is a formal word, so you will often meet it in reports, science and exams.
fact: Common phrases are detrimental to (something) and detrimental effect.
fact: «Smoking is detrimental to health.» means smoking harms your body.
fact: Everyday words with a similar meaning are harmful and bad for.
exercise: «Too much sugar is detrimental to your teeth.» What does detrimental mean? | Good for | *Harmful to | Shiny and clean | Sweet and tasty
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to detrimental? | bright | *harmful | helpful | quick
exercise: «Pollution has detrimental effects on rivers and fish.» What are the effects? | *Harm to rivers and fish | Clean water and happy fish | Bright colours in the water | Faster rivers
test: «Lack of sleep is detrimental to learning.» What does detrimental mean here? | *Bad for, causing harm | Easy to understand | Helpful to | Long and tiring
test: Which everyday words mean nearly the same as detrimental? | bright and shiny | soft and warm | quick and easy | *harmful and bad for
exam: Which sentence uses detrimental correctly? | The party was detrimental to the cake | *Smoking is detrimental to health | The sun was detrimental to the sky | My shoes are detrimental to the rain
